        "stated": "McNeely 2016: \"For the TAPS-1, any response other than 'never' constitutes a positive screen. Those with a positive screen complete the corresponding items on the TAPS-2.\" Gryczynski 2017 (PMID 28550609), abstract: \"Optimal frequency-of-use cut-points on the self-administered TAPS-1 for identifying SUDs were >= monthly use for tobacco and alcohol ... and any reported use for illicit drugs and prescription medication misuse.\""
